WEBVTT

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:04.830
A man's favourite cocktail has
to be the gin & tonic.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.960
And the ladies' favourite you ask?
The Spumoni, of course

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.760
Just like a single flower blooming in
the backstreets of Ginza...

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:46.180
You'd be forgiven for walking past
this place without noticing,

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.100
bar Eden hall.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:53.730
What cocktail would you like to enjoy
this evening, weary patron?

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:57.860
A Moscow Mule? Jack Rose?
A Nikolaschka maybe?

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:00.450
Or how about a Kir Royale?

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.450
How is one to choose?

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:09.250
That's when you ask the bartender,
"Excuse me, do you have a menu?"

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.880
But the answer you get is...

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.170
My apologies.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:18.300
Precisely.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:22.760
Most bars will either have no menu
or, if there is one,

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:23.970
it is nowhere in sight.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:25.970
The reason for this

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:32.520
is that presenting a list of names
to someone who doesn't know spirits...

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.360
is puite meaningless.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.950
I'm terribly sorry,
but we're closing for the night.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.380
But... there is also another reason
why bars don't have menus.

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.920
Please, could you help me find it?

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:00.090
My menu of the heart...

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:10.180
Find your menu of the heart, you say?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.270
Yes.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:15.690
I'm looking for the one drink in his heart
that he couldn't have 20 years ago,

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:18.110
because of me.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:24.280
The person who was supposed
to drink that was my grandfather.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:30.040
Grandpa.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.210
Grandpa.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.170
Grandpa!

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:40.170
Grandpa.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.020
The bottle in that paper bag...

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:02.400
Yes. That's it...

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:06.490
The menu of the heart that my grandfather
and I shared which I want you to find.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:10.580
Taizo Kurushima, my grandfather,

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.500
is the head of a fourth-generation
family of ryokan innkeepers.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:20.250
He is always very indulgent with me but
utterly stubborn when it comes to work.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.430
You see it in how particular he is
regarding cocktail recipes and service.

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.140
Framboise liqueur.

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:32.350
Rose wine.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.520
White curacao.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:36.270
Lime juice.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:37.940
And...

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:39.980
the shaker.

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.710
Please enjoy your Aphrodite.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.250
Mr Perfect.
Bartender, Ryuichi Kuzuhara.

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:05.760
His cocktails are truly perfection.

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:11.350
Whatever order my grandfather made,
his creations would bring him the answer.

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:16.520
The first time Mr Kurushima
drank an Aphrodite

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:20.270
was after the war,
when refrigerators were still a rarity.

00:05:20.610 --> 00:05:24.990
As such, you could not
cool drinks or glasses easily,

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.110
and so cocktails were not
as cold as they are nowadays.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:33.450
Which is why I took the liberty of making
Mr Kurushima's drink a little warm.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:37.120
Let's not forget one more important thing.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.340
Bartender, Minoru Higashiyama.

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:46.380
My grandfather was always awestruck
by the service this man offered.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:51.140
My Kurushima would
always enjoy his cocktails

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.760
in the company of his wife.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:57.730
But since his wife passed away,

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:01.230
Mr Kurushima has
come to enjoy the Aphrodite,

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:06.320
a cocktail whose name signifies
"eternal love".

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.320
Its beauty is found
not only in the flavour,

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:13.490
but perhaps also in who made it
and with whom one enjoyed it.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:18.410
Truly, it is those irreplaceable memories
that are what matters most.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:24.170
No matter how much time passes,
the memories of beauty remain.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:31.010
I do hope that our drinks might achieve
even a modicum of that beauty.

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:35.010
Spirits and memories like in the old days.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:39.390
Your grandfather
has fine taste in spirits.

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:42.400
But...

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.230
in the same season, each year,

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:48.740
my grandfather doesn't
even drink that cocktail.

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.030
It's my fault.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:04.340
When I was born,

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:08.210
all over Japan and its internationally
renowned metropoles,

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.010
a great many hotels began to spring up.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:15.760
Among these were
the long-standing traditional inns

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:17.810
that were relegated to the shadows.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:19.680
But my grandfather,

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.850
who doggedly clung on to the ryokan
service that had spanned generations,

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:28.570
was forever butting heads with my father,
who would one day take over the business.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:35.570
Father, please think carefully.
Times are changing!

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:37.990
It's now the era of urban hotels.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:41.370
Yet only your ryokan hasn't changed.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:46.500
I'm not saying that traditional inns
should be done away with entirely,

00:07:46.750 --> 00:07:49.340
only that clientele are now after
a new service style.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:53.340
If you keep clinging to
your traditional ways,

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.510
you'll run the family business
into the ground!

00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:58.640
That would be the final nail in the coffin
for ryokan inns!

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:05.730
Father!

00:08:11.610 --> 00:08:12.650
Father...

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:18.870
My grandfather realised that it was
a difficult time for ryokan in big cities.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.210
Which made it all the more difficult
for him to take his son's reprimands...

00:08:27.670 --> 00:08:30.300
A battle of wills that causes
a rift between father and son.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:31.880
Am I right?

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:32.970
Yes.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.720
My grandfather stood his ground and
refused to speak to my father after that.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:41.970
And, as if to differentiate his management
style from my grandfather's,

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:43.980
he went into the hotel industry,

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:46.850
which finally steadied
the Kurushima family business.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.570
Amidst all this, my grandfather
isolated himself more and more,

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:56.320
withdrawing from the management side
over time, and living a quiet life.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:00.780
Seeing this, my father felt
he needed to step in,

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:03.330
and tried to reconcile their differences.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:13.460
Father...

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:18.840
Actually, I found a bottle that
I would Iike you to try with me.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:20.970
Why?

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:25.230
Well... you'll know once you've tried it.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:28.520
Please. Just a sip.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:30.400
Just one.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.860
Even now, I still remember.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:36.990
It was when I was four years old.

00:09:37.700 --> 00:09:40.160
The first time our family
had ever had a party together.

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:45.830
But Grandfather wouldn't soften so easily
and struggled not to look uncomfortable.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.500
That's when,

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:54.250
my dad called his father over to drink
the spirits he'd struggled to find.

00:09:55.510 --> 00:09:59.930
Father, it took me forever to find
this bottle, come have a glass with me.

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:11.060
Grandpa!

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:13.820
Miwa...

00:10:45.260 --> 00:10:49.180
So that was the menu of the heart your
father and his were deprived of

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:50.690
twenty years ago.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:56.280
That incident caused their relationship
to remain stagnant,

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:59.490
and they were never
able to truly reconcile.

00:10:59.900 --> 00:11:03.490
Could you not just ask your father?

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.910
No, that's impossible.

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:08.790
My father...

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:13.040
passed away years ago.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:25.970
A little while after I broke that bottle,

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:29.100
I lost both my father and my mother.

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:34.400
I will never forget my grandfather's
expression when he heard the news.

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:40.360
After that, Grandfather totally changed
and threw himself into the hotel business.

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:45.410
The Kurushima ryokan grew into a vast
and well-reputed chain of hotels,

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:48.370
and I was raised
without want for anything.

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:50.870
Wrapped in my grandfather's love,

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:55.170
I grew into an adult, and remembered...

00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:59.590
the bottle that my father and grandfather
were supposed to drink together.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:06.890
Tomorrow is the anniversary
of my parents' death.

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:14.940
I was never scolded or told off
for breaking that bottle.

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:19.570
But I want to make amends nonetheless.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:24.240
If only I hadn't broken that bottle,
then perhaps...

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:28.620
Perhaps they could have
put aside their differences.

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:36.170
Very well.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.500
Let's think about it together.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:45.470
Thank you.

00:12:48.010 --> 00:12:50.640
What did your father like to drink?

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:53.140
Were there any foods he liked or disliked?

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:55.600
Or colours and scents he favoured?

00:12:56.400 --> 00:13:00.110
My only memories of my father date back
to when I was a small child...

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:01.820
They're a bit blurred.

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:05.650
In that case, let me ask
about the bottle you're looking for.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.700
For instance, was it a wine bottle?

00:13:12.040 --> 00:13:15.120
No. It felt more bumpy.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.370
Bumpy?

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.750
I seem to remember it
was very sparkly, as well.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:22.840
Maybe a crystal bottle?
Cognac?

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:26.050
For special occasions,
you might gift a Remy XIII.

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.140
If it was a Hennessy,
then perhaps Richard.

00:13:28.390 --> 00:13:30.930
No... with a name that means "landings"

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.600
the First Landing is a good choice
for reconciliations.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:41.360
In which case, there is
only one clue remaining...

00:13:42.730 --> 00:13:45.820
I found a bottle that
l would like you to try with me.

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:49.490
You'll know why after you've tried it.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:51.530
Please, take just one sip.

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:58.250
I believe you said your grandfather was
quite stubborn when it comes to alcohol.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:13:59.370
Yes.

00:13:59.830 --> 00:14:04.000
And the rift between him and his son was
due to his move into the hotel industry.

00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:09.220
A father and son confrontation.
Ryokan and hotels.

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.510
There is only one bottle
which fits that description.

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:17.020
Don't worry.

00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:18.230
You have it...?

00:14:19.480 --> 00:14:22.940
We have one bottle left in this bar.

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:29.610
And there it was in front of me once more,
the menu of my heart.

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:34.580
That was my curious first encounter
with bar Eden hall.

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.920
You picked a fine bottle.

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:49.930
Yes. I put myself in the young lady's
father's shoes when I chose it.

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.850
I thought of what I would want
to drink, if I were him.

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:59.350
And those memories dating back
20 years, which fill that bottle.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:03.480
I'm sure he will understand.

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:05.730
After all...

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.900
The hydrangea blossoms reflected
in the young lady's eyes.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:14.910
In the language of flowers they mean
"strong family bonds".

00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:48.570
One bottle for one menu of the heart.

00:15:49.690 --> 00:15:52.030
Why should that be a domestic whisky?

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:54.950
And in particular... Kaku?

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:58.330
It was the year 1923,

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:02.500
Shinjiro Torii of Kotobukiya Corp.,
known today as Suntory,

00:16:02.710 --> 00:16:06.590
invited Masataka Taketsuru, who had
studied Scotch distilling in Scotland,

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:10.510
and constructed the first ever distillery
in Yamazaki, Kyoto Prefecture.

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:15.550
However, the first-ever domestic whisky,
named "White Label",

00:16:15.930 --> 00:16:18.310
failed to impress the Japanese public.

00:16:20.020 --> 00:16:21.810
Indeed, that is true.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.980
The reason being that

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:28.110
Mr Taketsuru had wanted to recreate
a true Scotch, with peaty notes.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:32.780
Unfortunately, this was not a flavour
which the Japanese were accustomed to.

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:38.410
After that, Mr Taketsuru opened
his own distillery in Yoichi,

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.870
and established Nikka Whisky.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:43.710
In the meanwhile,

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:49.130
Shinjiro Torii continued in his quest
to find a whisky the Japanese could enjoy.

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:55.470
Symbolic of this is the turtle shell
pattern cut into the bottle.

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.140
The turtle, a symbol of
good luck to the Japanese.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.680
The cutting is modelled on

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:06.940
the Satsuma Glass Cutters techniques
which dates back to Japan's Edo period.

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:16.990
Which is probably the reason why
the bottle appeared to sparkle.

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:23.540
It is truly a whisky made
by the Japanese, for the Japanese.

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:34.920
Whisky may be a European spirit,

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:40.680
but it is possible to bottle it to suit
the palate and aesthetics of the Japanese.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:42.890
In the end,

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:48.140
all his departed son wanted to say was
that even if ryokan turn into hotels,

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:53.110
you can still offer your clientele
Japanese flavours and service standards,

00:17:56.650 --> 00:18:00.620
while sharing just one drink
with his beloved father.

00:18:18.970 --> 00:18:21.850
Thank you, Miwa. Thank you...

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:25.220
I know I caused you much pain too.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.560
I don't know what I can say...

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:29.890
Truly, thank you.

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:36.900
But, would you leave me alone
with this bottle just today?

00:18:37.740 --> 00:18:40.990
Looking back, I probably
worked furiously to try and forget

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:45.740
that terrible event that
took place 20 years ago now.

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:51.630
After he died, I tried to take his place
and build as many hotels as I could.

00:18:51.830 --> 00:18:55.250
In doing so, I thought that perhaps...

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:58.210
I could make it up to him somehow.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:02.050
And I would just like to know

00:19:02.220 --> 00:19:06.100
what he would say to me
if he could see me 20 years later.

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:08.770
What would he say, I wonder...?

00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:39.130
Though it is the same Kaku,
it no doubt tastes slightly different now.

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:42.800
It was in fact an old bottle
of Special Reserve.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:46.010
But why does it still taste different...?

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:52.060
The reason is that the water and wheat are
different, as are the production volumes.

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:55.650
There are a number of theories,
such as production becoming more refined,

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:59.650
or the in-bottle maturation
process having improved and suchlike.

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.450
Here is my theory.

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:09.790
The reason older bottles taste better,

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:13.210
is because they come filled
with irretrievable memories.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:18.340
Memories that remain locked in our hearts.

00:20:22.720 --> 00:20:24.800
Take the same whisky, for instance.

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:29.760
John straight, on the rocks, with water,
as a float or a mist.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:32.230
The styles vary greatly.

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:36.690
As well as the ice, the water
and the stirring method.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:42.990
Mixing other spirits,
one creates an ineffable menu.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:49.080
From all those choices, to open
the customer's heart and find out

00:20:49.370 --> 00:20:54.460
what it is they want to drink at that
moment, that is the job of the bartender.

00:20:56.120 --> 00:21:00.800
Which is why
the menu is found in one's heart.

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:13.770
RECIPE: BRANDY - To Taste
